================================================================================
WHAT THE MIT LICENSE ABOVE COVERS
================================================================================

The MIT license applies to MTEngineSDL's OWN code only:

    src/Engine/                 -- except src/Engine/Libs/ (see below)
    src/Embedded/
    platform/MacOS/src.MacOS/
    platform/Windows/src.Windows/
    platform/Linux/src.Linux/
    platform/MacOS/shaders/
    tools/
    tests/
    cmake/, CMakeLists.txt
    build-macos.sh, build-linux.sh, platform/*/build-*.sh, platform/*/build-*.ps1
    docs/

It does NOT apply to the bundled third-party components below. Those are the
property of their respective authors and are distributed under their own
licenses, which are reproduced inside their own directories.


================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
================================================================================

Third-party source lives in these locations, and NOTHING there is covered by
the MIT license above:

    src/Engine/Libs/            -- vendored libraries compiled into the engine
    other/lib/                  -- vendored/submoduled dependency source trees
    platform/MacOS/include/     -- SDL3 public headers
    platform/Windows/include/   -- SDL3 public headers
    platform/Windows/libs/      -- prebuilt third-party static archives

Each component carries its own license text in its own directory. The list
below names the ones whose terms are most likely to matter to you; it is a
convenience, not a substitute for reading those files.

  Component                       License
  ------------------------------  --------------------------------------------
  SDL2 / SDL3                     zlib
    other/lib/SDL-release-3.4.14-static/LICENSE.txt
    other/lib/SDL-release-2.32.10-static/LICENSE.txt
  Dear ImGui                      MIT
  Dear ImGui Test Engine          NOT OPEN SOURCE -- see the warning below
    src/Engine/Libs/imgui_test_engine/LICENSE.txt
  ImPlot                          MIT
  pugixml                         MIT
  libuv                           MIT           other/lib/libuv/LICENSE
  FTXUI                           MIT           other/lib/ftxui/LICENSE
  llama.cpp                       MIT           other/lib/llama.cpp/LICENSE
  uSockets / uWebSockets          Apache-2.0    other/lib/uSockets/LICENSE
  Basis Universal (transcoder)    Apache-2.0
    src/Engine/Libs/basis_universal/VENDORED.md
  Mbed TLS                        Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-or-later
    other/lib/mbedtls/LICENSE
  FreeType                        FTL OR GPL-2.0
    other/lib/freetype-2.10.4/docs/LICENSE.TXT
  Graphite2                       LGPL-2.1
    other/lib/graphite2-1.3.14/LICENSE
  LibRaw (image codecs)           CDDL-1.0 / LGPL-2.1
    fetched by platform/*/build-image_codecs.*; our patches are in
    other/lib/image-codecs/patches/ and are published as CDDL-1.0 requires

Not every component listed above is compiled into every build. MTEngineSDL is
capability-gated: an application's mtengine.caps manifest decides which
dependencies are fetched and linked at all. See docs/CAPABILITIES.md.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IMPORTANT: Dear ImGui Test Engine is not open source
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/Engine/Libs/imgui_test_engine/ is licensed by DISCO HELLO under the Dear
ImGui Test Engine License, NOT under MIT and NOT under any OSI-approved license.
It is free for you if you are a natural person, a non-profit, an educational
user, a project released publicly under an open source license, or a company
with under 2 million USD turnover in its last fiscal year. Otherwise it is a
45-day trial followed by a paid subscription from DISCO HELLO.

Read src/Engine/Libs/imgui_test_engine/LICENSE.txt before shipping a product
that includes it. It is reachable only through the MT_CAP_TEST_ENGINE
capability -- building with MT_CAP_TEST_ENGINE=0 excludes it entirely.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note on copyleft components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

FreeType, Graphite2, Mbed TLS and LibRaw offer copyleft licenses (GPL-2.0,
LGPL-2.1, CDDL-1.0) either exclusively or as one arm of a dual license. If you
link them statically into a closed-source product, the obligations are yours to
satisfy. Where a permissive arm exists (FTL for FreeType, Apache-2.0 for
Mbed TLS), choosing it is your decision to make and to record, not the engine's.
